      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**Field Technician's Guide: Installing and Operating the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor**\n\n**Before Starting**\n\nBefore proceeding with the installation, verify your Nexus Hub and ensure that your system is configured to recognize the Nexus Hub. This can typically be done by running the 'nexus-sync' command via terminal, waiting for a green LED blink to confirm successful synchronization with the hub.\n\n**Installation**\n\n1. Connect the Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor to the Nexus Hub via a USB-C cable.\n2. Mount the sensor to the standard bracket using an M3 screw, ensuring secure fastening.\n3. To perform the initial setup, hold the sensor 10cm from a flat surface and press the 'Calibrate' button for 3 seconds.\n\n**Calibration and Verification**\n\nDuring the calibration process, please exercise caution to avoid exposure to high-intensity UV light. Verify that the sensor is properly calibrated by checking the LED status:\n- Solid Green: Active sensor.\n- Blinking Green: Sensor is successfully syncing with the Nexus Hub.\n- Red: Indicate error or lack of power, and troubleshoot accordingly.\n\n**Safety Precautions**\n\n- Avoid submerging the sensor in liquid, as it may damage the electronic components.\n- Always adhere",
